Broken glass. It is never randomly generated, but appears when a potion, looking 
glass, or glass wand is shattered, or when a glass golem is killed. When a 
non-flying/floating creature other than buCEMPZ which does not have boots 
equipped steps on a tile containing it, there is a chance depending on the 
creature's dexterity/level and the size of the stack that it will step on the 
glass, slowing it for 3d4 turns and removing one piece from the game. Touching a 
piece of glass (rules for what constitutes touch are already defined for 
cockatrices) has a chance of dealing one point of damage. Polypiling may produce 
"worthless piece of [random color] glass" (7% chance) or a looking glass (1% 
chance), and counts towards glass golem creation, but otherwise stays the same.

